 # Mega Evolution work in progress
 
-This branch is an unfinished implementation, not playable Mega Evolution. It currently contains a battle-only form catalog and ownership/stat calculations for the native species whose listed form abilities and types already exist in the current game. Form stats, types, abilities and stone names come from pokeemerald-expansion-native bb3fd057061cdd7e6a9e79b76abb41924ee44ecc; this is not a wholesale Expansion port. The internal form and stone identifiers are not species or item IDs and must not be written to trainer saves.
+This draft is disabled and not playable. `MEGA_FEATURE_READY` defaults to 0. Do not merge, enable it for valuable saves, or treat its focused tests as a native build or gameplay verification.
 
-The state tracks one use per trainer and a trainer-local slot for an in-battle form, and computes transformed stats from level, IVs, EVs and nature while leaving HP and the underlying party untouched. It is not yet connected to move selection, actual held items or Key Stone acquisition, turn order, ability activation, sprites, switching, private reward restoration, link negotiation, or battle cleanup. Some existing Gen 3 abilities have different modern behavior. These gaps mean no Mega claim or release is appropriate.
+The battle-only form catalog covers 16 native species with types and abilities already present in the current game. Stats, types, abilities and stone names are adapted from pokeemerald-expansion-native bb3fd057061cdd7e6a9e79b76abb41924ee44ecc; this is not a wholesale Expansion port. Logical form identifiers are never written as party species. Existing Gen 3 abilities may differ from modern behavior.
 
-The actual next work is to connect selection and battle execution with owner validation and negotiated multiplayer compatibility; add real item/data and licensed or otherwise authorized art; maintain form across switching and revert at battle end/abort without mutating private party species; and expand the catalog alongside the actual newer ability/type implementation. Component tests exercise ownership and stat calculations only, not a native build, co-op runtime, persistence, or gameplay.
+The experimental path includes per-trainer selection and once-per-battle state, stat calculation from the party's level, IVs, EVs and nature, guarded move-choice transport and a matching native-link rule bit. When explicitly compiled with the gate enabled, a preliminary turn hook applies queued stats before moves, and the World menu has a settings toggle and a temporary stone-and-ring acquisition menu. These hooks are incomplete and must not be enabled: Form visuals and battle cleanup are not implemented or verified. A preliminary native controller event carries form identity and party slot to both players and waits for acknowledgements. The owning client gets move-selection eligibility from the master and checks its own Ring, with the master revalidating the choice. Actual multiplayer synchronization remains unverified. A preliminary ability sequence invokes existing switch-in ability effects and waits for their scripts, but it needs native gameplay verification and modern-mechanics review. A preliminary switch-in hook restores a form by trainer and battle-party slot without altering the underlying party; real switching and co-op ownership still need verification. The preliminary ordering also needs gameplay validation.
 
-The current working code also experiments with appending native-only item IDs 377–393 for stones and a Mega Ring, adds guarded move-choice transport and validates matching battle-rule capabilities. These IDs require a compatibility and migration decision before any real save uses them: older builds and Expansion have different item registries. Placeholder existing item icons are not final art. `MEGA_FEATURE_READY` defaults to 0; move selection cannot activate the unfinished feature. No native game build or real co-op test has been run.
+The working branch appends native-only item IDs 377–393 for stones and a Mega Ring. A save compatibility and migration strategy is required before real saves use them: older builds and Expansion have different item registries. Existing item icons are placeholders. Donor art has not been committed; its provenance and redistribution permissions need resolution.
+
+World > Gameplay settings contains the existing Party EXP, reusable TM and move-category toggles. All remain opt-in. Mega options are hidden while the feature gate is off.
+
+Component tests cover form calculations, trainer ownership, the game adapter and link rule matching with stubs. They do not establish native build success, actual co-op behavior, persistence, visuals or gameplay. The combined native candidate must be built and tested before release.
